## Reviewer got wrong (not applied)

- U+200B lines are not Catalan layout padding. They match the Korean source count exactly. Turning Q16–Q20 into new ## headings would also change the heading-level array. Both requests conflict with the checker and with the standing ban on new headings.
- The article-10 parenthetical is an editor’s note, but it is also the only Catalan carrier of the Korean link’s 제10조. Deleting it is not a free wording fix.
- «(1 vegada aquest import)» is a calque, and the prose already says the loss is the actual damage. The Korean sentence is still «최대 1배». The suggested rewrite without a 1 fails numbers. Applied as «fins a 1 vegada l’import del dany real» instead.
- Writing «un any» for a counted 1 is better Catalan. The checker’s ca lexicon does not parse un/una, so those digits stay.
- «TWD 1.57M» is an English decimal abbreviation. The standing rule pins that byte string; the surrounding «(1,57 milions de dòlars taiwanesos)» already gives the Catalan reading.
